StorageWorks RAID Array 230 Subsystem

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Hardware RAID subsystem for Alpha and Intel systems with PCI bus

o  PCI backplane RAID controller provides RAID levels 0 (striping), 1
   (mirroring), 0+1 (striped mirroring), and 5 (striping with parity)

o  Supports up to 21 disk drives per controller

o  Higher performance than the EISA based StorageWorks RAID Array 210
   Subsystem

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The StorageWorks RAID Array 230 subsystem is the second member of the
StorageWorks RAID Array 200 family, the first member being the StorageWorks
RAID Array 210 subsystem. (See the "StorageWorks RAID Array 210 Subsystem"
article in April 12, 1994 issue of Customer Update.) The StorageWorks RAID
Array 230 subsystem is functionally identical to the StorageWorks RAID Array
210 subsystem, but it includes a PCI backplane RAID controller instead of
the EISA backplane RAID controller found in the StorageWorks RAID Array 210
subsystem. The RAID utilities and the documentation are common to both
products, providing great flexibility in implementing RAID systems across
the enterprise.

PCI is a system bus that is gaining popularity on system servers because of
its higher performance than the EISA bus. The peak transfer rate of the PCI
bus is 132 MB per second. The peak transfer rate of the EISA bus is 32 MB
per second. Most Alpha and Intel systems include a PCI bus.

A StorageWorks RAID Array 230 subsystem is comprised of a PCI backplane RAID
controller, operating system specific RAID drivers and utilities (software),
documentation, and disk drives with appropriate cables and enclosures. The
controller provides the RAID functionality. It is a PCI backplane
controller, and plugs directly into the PCI bus inside the system enclosure.
Therefore, RAID functionality can be provided for the disk drives inside, as
well as outside, the system enclosure. Please refer to the Technical Data
section in this article for a list of supported systems.

BENEFITS

RAID provides increased performance and data reliability for disk
subsystems. Because it uses the PCI bus, the RAID Array 230 is a higher
performance subsystem than the RAID Array 210.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The StorageWorks RAID Array 230 subsystem can be configured with the disk
drives inside the system enclosure, or in standalone configurations, where
the disk devices are contained in StorageWorks pedestal enclosures. In
either case, the StorageWorks RAID Array 230 subsystem is configured by a
simple "sum of the pieces" scheme that vastly reduces the number of
orderable parts, and provides growth and configuration flexibility.

A StorageWorks RAID Array 230 Subsystem consists of the following key
components:

o  A KZPSC PCI backplane RAID controller, which includes the appropriate
   software and documentation kit
o  StorageWorks disk drives
o  Enclosures, as required, to house the disks
o  Cables to connect the controller to the disk drives
o  Additional StorageWorks components (redundant power supplies, fans, etc.)

The KZPSC backplane RAID controller is available in two models, a single
SCSI channel variant that supports up to 7 disk drives, and a three channel
model that supports up to 21 drives.

