Performance

The performance of a RAID subsystem is dependant on a large number of
parameters, including RAID level, RAID subsystem specific attributes (type
and size of cache), number of RAID controllers on the system, number and
type of disks used, application parameters (read/write ratio, file size, and
block size, etc.), type of system, overall system activity, operating
system, and many others, so it is very difficult to specify performance
attributes.

Performance testing in a user environment indicates that the performance of
a StorageWorks RAID Array 210 subsystem (EISA based) EISA ranges from 150 to
350 I/Os per second for an application using a balanced mix of read and
writes in a RAID 5 configuration. Preliminary tests indicate that in the
same environment, the StorageWorks RAID Array 230 subsystem (PCI based) will
see a twofold performance improvement.

