Next Generation, 4-mm Digital Audio Tape (DAT) Loader Subsystems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides up to 96 GB of capacity

o  Is ideal for unattended backup of workstations and servers

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The DDS-2 compliant, 4-mm TLZ7L DAT Loader provides up to 96 GB of
unattended backup and archiving capability, with a transfer rate of up to
810 KB per second. The DAT Loader provides up to 32 GB of unattended
capacity with its standard 4-cartridge magazine, and up to 96 GB of
unattended backup with its optional 12-cartridge magazine. The TLZ7L is also
read/write compatible with the media used in the TLZ06 and TLZ6L loaders,
and the TLZ04 and TLZ07 drives.

BENEFITS

o  High Unattended Backup Capacity -- The DDS-2 format of the TLZ7L provides
   a native unattended capacity of 4 GB, and a compressed capacity of 8 GB,
   an effective match for many of today's small servers.

o  Multiple Loader Options -- With its standard four-cartridge and optional
   12-cartridge magazines, the TLZ7L can be tailored to meet user needs.

o  First Generation Read/Write Compatibility -- The TLZ7L can read and write
   both DDS-2 and DDS-1 media, ensuring investment protection as well as
   data interchange with DDS-1 drives.

o  Multiple Packaging Options -- The TLZ7L is available in system-installed,
   tabletop, and StorageWorks versions, enabling wide-spread user adoption
   and convenience.

o  Media Quality Checking -- The TLZ7L implements the new DDS-2 media
   recognition system, eliminating the performance and service issues
   related to use of audio-grade media cartridges.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The TLZ7L DAT Loader will be available as of March 13, 1995 through Digital
and its business partners. Five copies of media, a cleaning cartridge, and a
four-cartridge magazine are included with all models.

