DEChub ONE-MX Single Slot Hub for DEChub 900 Modules

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides redundant power capability for all existing and planned "rack
   and stack," standalone DEChub 900 modules

o  Supports FDDI ModPMD ports for PEswitch 900TX modules when used in a
   single slot, rack and stack configuration

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The DEChub ONE-MX is a flexible single slot hub chasis providing 90 watts of
power for attached DEChub 900 modules. When two DEChub ONE-MX units are
configured in a "piggy-back" fashion with a power cable connected between
them, the new hub offers automatic redundant power failover capability for
all existing and planned DEChub 900 modules.

For existing DEChub 900 Ethernet modules, network connectivity is supported
through an AUI port for connecting to a standard Ethernet backbone as well
as an out-of-band management port. FDDI, which is currently supported only
by the PEswitch 900TX, is provided through two modular PMD (Physical Media
Dependent) ports. For FDDI applications, the DEChub ONE-MX utilizes the
existing FDDI ModPMD (Modular PMD) ports (Single Mode Fiber, Multi Mode
Fiber, and UTP cable) used on Digital's GIGAswitch product and
DECconcentrator 900MX modules. When used with all DEChub 900 modules, the
DEChub ONE-MX hub provides redundant power for these standalone rack and
stack applications, meeting the user need for fault tolerance in a stackable
product.

BENEFITS

o  Provides a redundant power option for standalone DEChub 900 product
   applications when the fault tolerance power is critical.

o  Allows PEswitch 900TX FDDI ports to be used in a standalone, single slot,
   rack and stack configuration.

PRODUCT POSITIONING

Providing redundant power and FDDI support, the new DEChub ONE-MX is a
higher-end version of the existing DEChub ONE single slot hub (DEHUA-C*).
The DEChub ONE-MX (DEF1H) is backwards-compatible with the current DEChub
ONE. All full-height modules will be able to utilize the new single slot hub
chasis as well as the redundant power capabilities. A firmware upgrade may
be needed for the module itself in order to utilize limited HUBwatch
capabilities. The DECconcentrator 900MX and DECswitch 900EF will be able to
access the FDDI ports with a firmware upgrade that will be available in May.

FDDI Single Mode Fiber (SMF) is supported through the SMF PMD slots
(DEFXS-AA), and can be installed in both PMD slots simultaneously. Caution
must be used when installing the SMF PMD slots to ensure that the fiber does
not exceed the break radius. Digital recommends that a qualified service
person perform the installation of all ModPMD slots.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The DEChub ONE-MX is available now through Digital; its DECdirect service;
and its authorized resellers, VARs, OEMs and wholesale distributors.
Digital's DEChub ONE products have a convenient return-to-Digital one-year
warranty. The user simply returns the product to Digital by mail, and within
30 days receives a replacement product. Additional years of return-to-
factory service are available. Optionally, onsite services can be purchased
that provide product replacement within a maximum of 24 hours.

