Remote Server Mgr, Dial-up Management of EISA Based Prioris Servers

HIGHLIGHTS

o     Remote management, maintenance, and control of distributed servers to
reduce costly service calls and optimize uptime

o    Server fault monitoring and control from management station via dial-up

o   Remote console and remote diskette features that enable the operator to
reset, reconfigure, and downline load server in a fault condition

o      Automatically alerts system manager of fault conditions and logs all
events

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Remote Server Manager lets administrators manage EISA based servers from one
system independent platform regardless of the server's operating system or
location. It combines a reliable link to the server with monitoring and
control.

Remote Server Manager is an integrated hardware and software solution to
remotely access, manage, maintain, and control distributed servers from a
management station or console. Its continuous monitoring, full remote
control, efficient fault resolution capabilities, ability to simultaneously
manage multiple servers, and ease of use help optimize uptime and reduce
support costs. The need to travel to remote sites can be virtually
eliminated by having remote monitoring and control capabilities.

Key features of Remote Server Manager include: Remote Console, Remote
Diskette, Operating System Independence, Security, and Alerts and Pager.
Remote Console enables the system manager, via the management station, to
remotely access and take control of the managed server console. Remote
Diskette allows a managed server's diskette drive to be remotely controlled
and booted using a diskette from the management station.

Three levels of security can be implemented with Remote Server Manager. The
system manager can set up alerts to notify if an abnormal or exception
condition is detected. If the administrator is away from the management
station, the pager feature can be used to contact them.

The EISA module communicates through a modem connection with the management
station and monitors the vital signs of the server, including the
temperature, voltage, system status, and more. The hardware card will
initiate communication with the management station, alerting it of events or
problems. This is independent of whatever operating system is running on the
server.

Digital's Remote Server Manager consists of the following products:

o  Remote Server Manager Hardware Kit -- This is required for each server
   managed. The kit includes an intelligent EISA bus master controller, a
   data cable, power supply, power cord, and keyboard jumper cable.

o  Remote Server Station Management Software -- The software is loaded into
   a management station personal computer. The minimum requirements are:
   - Personal computer using an Intel 386/486 microprocessor
   - Windows NT V3.1 or higher
   - Hard disk with 4 MB of available space
   - 3.5-inch high-density (1.44 MB) disk drive
   - Hayes-compatible modem with V.42 error correction
   - CD-ROM
   - SVGA video adapter
   - Buffered serial port with a 16550 UART chip

In addition to the minimum requirements, Digital recommends:
   - 16 MB additional memory
   - Windows NT compatible mouse or pointing device
   - WIndows NT compatible printer

For convenience, Digital offers a Remote Server Manager System package that
has both the hardware kit and management software. This package is offered
for those users getting started using Remote Server Manager.

For each hardware kit (including the system package), the user must order a
cable kit, which depends on which server platform the card will be
installed. An external modem also is required at each server. This allows
the system administrator the ability to dial into the modem and get status
of the server even if the server power is off. An optional UPS also is
offered.

BENEFITS

o  Central monitoring and control of remote servers -- This reduces cost by
   using the multitasking capabilities of Windows NT, which enables multiple
   sessions running simultaneously on one management station. It offers
   remote boot, remote power on and off, file transfer, and remote diskette.

o  Server operating system independent -- Users only need one package to
   monitor servers running most major operating systems.

o  Environmental sensors to alert system administrator -- These monitor the
   internal and external voltage of the server, power, and POST. Internal
   temperature also can be monitored, alerting the management station prior
   to overheating.

o  Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) Interface -- PPP is an efficient,
   industry-standard communication over phone lines, which ensures that even
   though the network may be down, users linked to the server will stay
   active.

o  Remote diagnostics and POST -- The Remote Server Manager runs diagnostics
   and displays Power On self test on the remote console prior to sending
   technician, saving time and unnecessary service calls.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Remote Server Manager Package, which includes server hardware and Remote
Server Management Station software, is available now. The software is
available in English, French, and Spanish.

For each Remote Server Manager hardware kit or Remote Server Manager system
package, users must order a cable kit related to the server platform.

