AdvantageCluster Available Server System Model 5004/275

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Fully configured cabinet system combines DECsafe Available Server
   software with two AlphaServer 2100 4/275 RM symmetric multi-processing
   (SMP) systems to support high availability applications

o  Server system is easily expanded by adding up to three more CPUs per SMP
   node, and/or by adding additional nodes

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Designed to support high availability applications, the AdvantageCluster
Available Server (ACAS) cabinet system Model 5004/275 is fully configured
with two DEC OSF/1 based AlphaServer 2100 4/275 RM (rackmount) systems in
one cabinet, and a storage shelf ready for disks.

Each AlphaServer 2100 4/275 RM system comes in a single processor
configuration with a 2 GB RZ28 internal system disk, 128 MB of memory, DEC
OSF/1 operating system, and DECsafe Available Server software. Also included
are the Logical Storage Manager and POLYCENTER Advanced File System
Utilities to provide flexible storage allocation and management. The
5004/275 systems do not include keyboard, monitor, mouse, or NAS 200
software.

Systems are designed for easy expansion up to four SMP processors per node,
and up to four BA350 storage shelves, each holding up to six 3.5-inch disks.
The cabinet can also be expanded with additional storage, a tape loader, or
other equipment.

System Configuration

o  Two AlphaServer 2100 4/275 RM systems (DA-252W1-F9) with DEC OSF/1 and
   server licenses, a 2 GB disk, and 128 MB of memory.
o  One TLZ07 8 GB DAT tape drive.
o  One set of documentation and two licenses for DECsafe Available Server
   software (QB-05SAG-AA and QL-05SAG-AA).
o  Two licenses of Logical Storage Manager software (QL-2GVAG-AA).
o  Two licenses of POLYCENTER Advanced File System Utilities software
   (QL-0EGAG-AA).
o  One 170 cm ANSI/EIA cabinet (H9A10-CG/CH) with two power controllers.
o  One BA350 StorageWorks storage shelf.
o  Two 2 GB, 3.5-inch SCSI disks (RZ28-VA).
o  Two KZPSA Fast Wide Differential SCSI controllers.
o  SCSI cabling and terminations.

