LinkWorks V3.0 -- The Solution Framework

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Adds an object-oriented development and deployment environment to the
   existing LinkWorks V2.1 functionality

o  Scripts, application programming interfaces, and software components
   allow for the creation of customized solutions

o  Improved user interface, workflow, performance, scalability, and system
   administration

o  Built-in integration for several mail clients, ALL-IN-1 access, and X.500
   directory services

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

LinkWorks software is Digital's award-winning Solution Framework for the
workgroup environment. It is employed by users worldwide to streamline their
business processes and to improve team productivity. It is the world's first
Solution Framework to be fully object-oriented and enterprise deployable.

The LinkWorks product group-enables existing systems with group-sharing,
document management, and workflow functionality. With V3.0, the fully
object-oriented LinkWorks engine is open to the outside world. This allows
for the development and deployment of group-enabled client/server solutions
and for the integration of business applications and legacy systems with the
LinkWorks Solution Framework.

To build horizontal or vertical solutions upon LinkWorks software, the
following tools can be used:

o  LinkWorks Scripts -- This is a BASIC like language that can also be used
   to automatically record, edit, and replay sequences of user actions.

o  Applications Plus Objects -- Extensive and powerful application
   programming interfaces (APIs) can extend external applications with
   LinkWorks functionality. The APIs support interaction between
   applications and LinkWorks objects in the areas of navigation, attribute
   access, object action, and drag and drop. They use industry-standard
   mechanisms such as DDE, OLE2, and DLL/shared libraries.

o  Software Components -- Available from Digital business partners or
   independent software vendors, these solutions extend LinkWorks software
   with additional functionality. Sophisticated technology allows for the
   extraction into a software component object of all the elements of a
   tailored solution. The software component can then be distributed (e.g.,
   by mail or through the Internet) and installed through runtime
   drag-and-drop. LinkWorks software includes a comprehensive graphical
   workbench, including browser, debugger, and profiler.

The Software Developer's Kit consists of the following items to help
developers build value-added solutions on top of LinkWorks software:

o  Documentation for the application developer, including an Introduction to
   LinkWorks Solution Development, the Class Programming Guide, the APO
   Reference Guide, and the Configuration Guide

o  Twenty small example applications and 30 code fragments

o  Extensive online help for the application developer

o  Sources for the user online help

The Software Developer's Kit does not contain the LinkWorks development
software which is packaged with the product itself. The kit is Windows
installable and comes in English only.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

LinkWorks V3.0 is available now. Packages include license, media, and
documentation.

The initial release of LinkWorks V3.0 will consist of the English language
version of the DEC OSF/1 server with support for the ORACLE and INGRES
databases and for the Windows 3.1 client. The Finnish, French, German,
Hungarian, Italian, Portuguese, and Swedish language versions will be
available in March 1995, and the remaining language versions will be
available in April 1995.

Most of the remaining platforms will be released in two waves during the
first half of 1995. Wave 1 will include the OS/2 client and the following
server platforms: Intel SCO UNIX, DEC OSF/1 INGRES and INFORMIX, HP-UX
INFORMIX and ORACLE, and IBM AIX ORACLE. Wave 2 will include the Macintosh
client and the following servers: Windows NT Intel ORACLE and OpenVMS AXP
ORACLE.

The Motif clients, as well as the Windows 95 and Mobile/OCC clients, are
scheduled for the second half of 1995. The Software Developer's Kit and the
User Guide Source Kit will be available in April 1995.

Please note that the order numbers are version independent. LinkWorks V2.1
for the Windows client and DEC OSF/1 server will stay orderable as LinkWorks
software requires that all clients and servers in a domain are the same
version. When ordering the V2.1 release (because the project needs immediate
Macintosh or Motif client support), the version number needs to be mentioned
explicitly -- or V3.0 will be delivered.

Alternate order numbers need to be used for Eastern European languages
(Czech, Hungarian, Russian, and Slovak). Use the following UPI
substitutions: 118 = 11C, 3EK = 37D, 11D = 2D6, 3E5 = 3E9, and 3RD = 3RE.

Licensing Model Changes

With V3.0, LinkWorks server licensing changes from the current traditional
licenses to a PC-style, platform-specific licensing model. This provides the
following options:

o  Server License -- Platform specific and language independent

o  Server Package -- Includes license and media and documentation kit;
   platform and language specific

o  Client License -- Generic client license; platform and language
   independent

o  Client Package -- Includes license and media and documentation kit;
   platform and language specific

Media and documentation kits will no longer be available separately.

