Oracle7 and Rdb Database Product Families Now Available from Digital

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Digital can now resell the entire Oracle family of database products,
   including the Oracle7 and Oracle Rdb product families

o  Rdb runtime functionality removed from OpenVMS VAX and existing NAS
   packages

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

On November 30, 1994, Digital and Oracle Corporation finalized an agreement
under which Digital sold its Rdb products to Oracle. An important part of
this agreement is Digital's opportunity to resell -- as an Oracle Business
Alliance Partner -- the entire family of Oracle database products, including
both the Oracle7 and Oracle Rdb product families. As a result, Digital sales
representatives are now able to resell the Oracle database products
individually as well as through value-added packages.

On February 6, 1995, Digital began reselling the Oracle family of database
products -- including the Oracle7 and Oracle Rdb product sets -- with new
part numbers, prices, and Oracle Corporation terms and conditions. Existing
Digital part numbers and prices for the Digital Rdb family of products went
into maintenance on February 13, 1995.

Overview

Initially, Digital will offer the latest versions of Oracle's most popular
database products, including Oracle7, associated tools, and Oracle's
Cooperative Development Environment (CDE) and CASE products. Additionally,
popular AdvantageServer packages will be configured with the appropriate
entry-level license, offering a convenient base platform for building a
customized solution. All of Oracle's offerings (on all platforms) are
available for System Integration business.

The following Oracle7 family of products are now available through Digital:

Oracle7 Database Products       Cooperative Development Environment Products
- Parallel Query Option		- Oracle Forms
- Parallel Server Option	- Oracle Reports
- Replication Option		- Oracle Graphics
- Distributed Option		- Oracle Book
- SQL*Textretrieval		- Oracle Data Browser
- SQL*Net			- SQL*Plus
Oracle in Motion:		- Oracle Data Query
- Message Gateway		- Oracle Precompiler
- Agent Event Manager		- SQL*Module
Gateways:			CASE Products:
- Transparent Gateway/Rdb	- Oracle CASE Library
- Transparent Gateway/RMS	- Oracle CASE Designer
Oracle Server Manager		- Oracle Forms Generator
				- Oracle Report Generator

All of the Oracle7 products are supported on OpenVMS VAX, OpenVMS Alpha, and
DEC OSF/1 systems.

Following is a list of the Oracle Rdb family of products as they existed
while owned by Digital verus their new Oracle names:

Previous Digital Name		 New Oracle Name

DEC Rdb				 Oracle Rdb
DEC DBMS			 Oracle CODASYL DBMS
DEC Rally			 Oracle Rally
CDD/Repository			 Oracle CDD/Repository
CDD/Administrator		 Oracle CDD/Administrator
DEC RdbExpert			 Oracle Expert for Rdb
DEC Instant SQL			 Oracle InstantSQL for Rdb
DEC Graphical Schema Editor	 Oracle Graphical Schema Editor for Rdb
DECtrace			 Oracle Trace
DEC ODBC Driver			 Oracle ODBC Driver for Rdb

In general, these products have a one-to-one mapping of functionality from
old environment to new environment. The exception is the Oracle Rdb product.
Previously, DEC Rdb was sold with either a runtime, interactive, or
development level of functionality. Now, Oracle Rdb essentially has the
"runtime" functionality level of the Rdb product. To obtain increased
functionality to create an "interactive" or "development" style of product
offering, Oracle has created several additional functional offerings that
can be added to the base Oracle Rdb offering.

Specifically, these offerings are:

o SQL/Services Protocol (choice of DECnet, TCP/IP, etc.)
o Oracle Rdb SQL Precompilers (choice of FORTRAN, COBOL, C, etc.)
o Oracle Module Language
o Oracle RDBPRE Precompilers (choice of FORTRAN, COBOL, etc.)

Effective February 6, the right to use Rdb runtime functionality is no
longer included with OpenVMS VAX Operating User Licenses ("001"). The Rdb
runtime and DECtrace functionality has been removed from the NAS Packages
effective with V6.0.

Oracle Rdb V6.1 will be available in March. Features of this new version
will include support for DEC OSF/1 systems, performance enhancements (25
percent faster in many cases), VLDB (Very Large Database) cache support,
support for Windows NT and DEC OSF/1 clients, and improved ease of use with
a new graphical user interface for Rdb Management Utility (RMU).

BENEFITS

Oracle and Digital have entered into an advanced Strategic Relationship
Agreement that allows Digital to resell the full suite of Oracle products.
This offers one-stop shopping for Digital users looking for the industry's
leading database and server solution, and will result in greater levels of
user satisfaction over time.

Existing and future Rdb software users will benefit from the increased
development investments that Oracle will make in the Rdb product set.
Because the Rdb engineering and support team has been largely retained by
Oracle, users can rely on the continuing availability of high-quality
development and support resources.

Oracle's popular Oracle7 relational database and associated tools are now
available from Digital. The Oracle advanced Parallel Options and Distributed
Option allow for the utilization of relational technology in large database
and heavy-demand applications. Coupled with Oracle's Cooperative Development
Environment products, these options enable users to develop sophisticated
applications that will capture the essence of state-of-the-art software
development -- from a robust CASE environment to time-saving form and report
generation products.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Oracle7 and Oracle Rdb database products are available through Digital
and its DECdirect service; Oracle Rdb products are also available through
Digital's resellers.

