EduLink V1.0 for Enhanced Work Integration and Collaboration in Education

HIGHLIGHTS

o  A client/server software package designed to enhance work integration and
   collaboration within schools and school systems

o  Helps the education community structure and allocate its scarce resources
   and work efforts among students, teachers, staff, and administrators

o  A foundation for delivering custom solutions that integrates personal,
   instructional, administrative, Internet access, and groupware
   applications with a common graphical user interface

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

EduLink V1.0 is an application integration framework, built specifically for
schools, that connects applications, people, and information in a local area
network. The software integrates the work of a school or school system,
enabling greater levels of collaboration than previously possible.

EduLink software can integrate most kinds of applications that educators and
students want to use. V1.0 provides extensive group communication facilities
that allow easy sharing of information, created by these applications, with
other educators and students. EduLink software streamlines the
people-intensive tasks that are common in working with school boards,
departments, classes, and faculties. The product's highly graphical
front-end makes this integration possible with a level of simplicity that
allows users to take advantage of the benefits of client/server computing.
The software provides integration capabilities with extensive data security
features that meet requirements for good data management, and management of
user access to data and applications within the school or school system.

BENEFITS

EduLink V1.0 is based on the LinkWorks application framework. In the same
way that the LinkWorks framework enables users to build automated project
and process solutions, EduLink V1.0 enables educators to define
organizational structure and processes, thereby managing how users
collaborate to meet the system's goals. The software provides teachers and
administrators with levels of control not possible with standalone PCs or
lower-level network operating systems.

Other benefits include:

o  Makes data immediately available to the appropriate workgroup members
   (students, faculty, etc.) within a well managed, secure environment.

o  Allows for more rapid solution development than other environments,
   enabling educators to quickly tailor the standard EduLink offering to
   meet their specific needs -- often without any IS involvement.

o  Responds to the desire for increased freedom and flexibility by allowing
   a managed choice of desktop and personal applications.

o  Enables greater work efficiency; work management capabilities allow
   workgroup members -- whether they be students, teachers, or
   administrators -- to easily establish collaborative groupings as needed.
   Other workgroup software requires administrative interventions to
   accomplish the same thing.

o  Provides all of these features on heterogeneous client workstations and
   open, industry-standard server operating systems and architectures.

o  Provides Internet utilities both for browsing and creating Mosaic and
   Netscape Home Pages for the school or school system.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

EduLink V1.0 is now available to educators (only) worldwide through Digital
and its business partners. The product can be ordered as either a standalone
system (Standard EduLink), which requires that a database management system
be already installed, or packaged with the Oracle7 database on DEC OSF/1
software (EduLink and Oracle7 Server Package).

Standard EduLink V1.0 for OpenVMS Alpha or DEC OSF/1 based servers requires
that the Oracle7 database be already installed. Standard EduLink V1.0 for
SCO UNIX based servers requires that the INFORMIX database be already
installed.

EduLink clients are available in five-packs only. EduLink servers are
available in single-packs. Discount Curve "C" applies to all EduLink V1.0
purchases.

