DECwindows Motif V1.2-3 for OpenVMS

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Incorporates the Open Software Foundation's OSF/Motif Release 1.2.3
   Toolkit and MIT X11 Release 5 (X11R5); and contains the NCSA Mosaic
   browser

o  On VAX systems, requires OpenVMS VAX V5.5-2 or greater; on Alpha systems,
   requires OpenVMS Alpha V1.5 or greater

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DECwindows Motif V1.2-3 for OpenVMS VAX and Alpha systems (SPD 42.19)
provides:

o  The Open Software Foundation's OSF/Motif Release 1.2.3 Toolkit, which
   contains more than 600 software fixes.

o  The National Center for Supercomputer Applications (NCSA) Mosaic browser,
   a World Wide Web browser that allows you to navigate and access
   information on the Internet.

o  Easier installation of DECwindows Motif software using the POLYCENTER
   Software Installation utility, which enables users to easily install and
   track software products on their systems.

o  A console window application that lets users display operator messages
   without toggling between DECwindows Motif windows and the workstation
   console window.

Important Changes

o  To encourage new applications to be written to the current Motif
   standard, DECwindows Motif V1.2-3 does not include XUI, OSF/Motif Release
   1.1.3, or OSF/Motif Release 1.2.2 programming support. Application
   development is supported for the current OSF/Motif Release 1.2.3 Toolkit
   only. However, users can choose to save the XUI or OSF/Motif Release
   1.1.3 programming environment during the installation of DECwindows Motif
   V1.2-3.

   Digital will continue to ship the appropriate runtime libraries for
   applications built against (compiled and linked with) XUI, OSF/Motif
   Release 1.1.3, or OSF/Motif Release 1.2.2 in the DECwindows Motif V 1.2-3
   layered product. Thus, existing users will continue to be able to run
   existing applications built against XUI, OSF/Motif Release 1.1.3, or
   OSF/Motif Release 1.2.2 libraries in a DECwindows Motif V 1.2-3
   environment.

o  The OSF/Motif Release 1.1.3 and Release 1.2.3 Toolkits, on which the
   DECwindows Motif V1.1 and V1.2-3 layered products are respectively based,
   are incompatible. However, applications built against the OSF/Motif
   Release 1.1.3 Toolkit will continue to run without modification under
   DECwindows Motif V1.2-3 because DECwindows Motif V1.1 shareable libraries
   will continue to ship with the DECwindows Motif V1.2-3 layered product.

   Applications built against the OSF/Motif Release 1.2.2 Toolkit (on which
   DECwindows Motif V1.2 is based) will also continue to run without
   modification under DECwindows Motif V1.2-3.

   Note that only those applications that have been built against the
   OSF/Motif Release 1.2.3 Toolkit can take advantage of the more than 600
   software fixes that have been made to the OSF/Motif Release 1.2.3
   Toolkit.

   In most cases, simple applications (for example, those that contain no
   private toolkit routines or user-written widgets) built against the
   OSF/Motif Release 1.1.3 Toolkit can just recompile and relink against the
   new OSF/Motif Release 1.2.3 Toolkit to pick up improvements. However,
   previously unseen errors in a DECwindows Motif V1.1 application may be
   exposed by relinking against the new DECwindows Motif V1.2-3 Toolkit, and
   behavior and widget layout changes in the V1.2-3 Toolkit may require
   other modifications to a user's application.

o  For the foreseeable future, the Bookreader viewer will continue to be the
   OpenVMS default online documentation viewer. The Interleaf WorldView
   Viewer will not be packaged with the DECwindows Motif for OpenVMS layered
   product. Bookreader files for viewing OpenVMS and DECwindows Motif
   documentation will continue to be delivered through the CONOLD
   (consolidated online documentation) service. Digital will also continue
   to use DECdocument and DECwrite to develop Bookreader files.

o  DEClinks, formerly known as LinkWorks, is no longer a supported
   DECwindows Motif feature. Support for DEClinks is removed from the
   Session Manager, the desktop applications menus, and the out-of-the-box
   (OOTB) desktop applications.

o  DECsound is supported only on TURBOchannel systems, including: DEC 3000
   Model 400, Model 500, Model 700, and Model 900 series; and VAXstation
   4000 Models VLC, 60, and 90. DECsound is not supported on the DEC 2000
   Model 300 series, the AlphaStation 200, or AlphaStation 400.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DECwindows Motif V1.2-3 for OpenVMS VAX and Alpha software is available now.
The software is currently available for OpenVMS Alpha systems via quarterly
distribution on CD-ROM; and will be available for OpenVMS VAX systems via
quarterly distribution on CD-ROM in March.

The DECwindows Motif software is factory installed on all AlphaStation and
VAXstation systems. The DECwindows Motif license Product Authorization Key
(PAK) is packaged with the AlphaStation and VAXstation systems and is
included on the Bill of Materials (BOM). Users purchasing a Factory
Installed Software (FIS) system are strongly urged to order the DECwindows
Motif media.

The DECwindows Motif Programming Documentation Kit has been revised for this
V1.2-3 release and applies to DECwindows Motif software on both the VAX and
Alpha  platforms. DECwindows Motif users who obtain DECwindows Motif
binaries and documentation on CD-ROM will receive both user and most
programming documentation in Bookreader format.

