DECADMIRE - V2.1, V2.1 for Visual Basic, and V3 Program Announcement

HIGHLIGHTS

o  DECADMIRE V2.1 for Visual Basic extends Microsoft's Visual Basic
   development environment by generating Visual Basic client/server
   applications (ODBC or ACMS Desktop based)

o  New Windows based development environment has been added to DECADMIRE
   software

o  Special introductory 35 percent discount on DECADMIRE for Visual Basic
   and DECADMIRE for Visual Basic/TP workgroup packages now available
   worldwide -- through July 1995

o  Program announcement of DECADMIRE V3.0, the development environment of
   which will support multiple platforms (DEC OSF/1, Windows NT, Windows95,
   and MAC) and any ODBC compliant database

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DECADMIRE V2.1 for Visual Basic software provides a development framework
linked to Microsoft's Visual Basic product. The software allows developers
to define or modify a default application architecture, setup and modify
project templates, and generate the application based on Visual Basic Forms
and code.

DECADMIRE V2.1 for Visual Basic software automatically generates the complex
code logic needed to merge the client and server software into a robust
application. The product allows developers to work entirely in a Windows
environment on the PC, building and testing their client/server
applications.

DECADMIRE V2.1 for Visual Basic software utilizes the robust Visual Basic
development environment for prototyping, debugging, and maintaining the
generated application components. The software offers a complete, rapid
client/server application development environment that allows the generation
of client/server applications based on standard ODBC, Digital's mature third
generation languages, ACMS, and database technology -- such as Visual Basic
ODBC for Oracle Rdb, Oracle, Microsoft SQL SERVER, or Access software.

The DECADMIRE V2.1 classic base product design has been modified to allow
shared development of data and modules between character cell (DECforms) and
Windows (Visual Basic) based applications.

Single to enterprise packages are available for small to large development
teams.

DECADMIRE V2.1 for Visual Basic Features

o  Provides a new Windows based development environment.

o  Offers client/server development utilizing an OpenVMS based server with a
   common development repository.

o  Generates Visual Basic application objects, form definitions, code
   procedures, and project files.

o  Can be deployed with Digital's Alpha (Windows NT, DEC OSF/1, OpenVMS
   systems) or VAX servers running ODBC or ACMS Desktop software.

o  Utilizes Digital's third generation languages and ACMS products in the
   OpenVMS server environment to offer full transaction processing.

o  Provides automatic re-generation and added maintenance controls.

o  Generates timeshare (via third generation languages, DECforms) or classic
   OLTP applications.

DECADMIRE V3.0 Program Announcement

DECADMIRE V3.0 will allow developers to work independent of the platform on
which they want to deploy their application. They will be able to test and
prototype application definitions, logic, and database interaction on PCs.

With V3.0, the framework established with Microsoft's Visual Basic software
will become more formalized, taking advantage of new and exciting Visual
Basic features to create a seemless development environment.

In addition, a high speed transport will be made available between the
client and server, which will utilize both Digital's ACMS Desktop and ACMSxp
client/server TP monitor software on DEC OSF/1 and Windows NT based systems.
V3.0 will also generate stored procedures, STDL (Standard Test Definition
Language) programs, and ACMSxp applications based on STDL.

BENEFITS

An excellent way to enter the world of open systems with little risk is to
use DECADMIRE software as the development tool for a new client/server
application. Once an application has been defined to DECADMIRE software, it
can be generated into any of the following runtime environments without
requiring a change to the definition:

o  A two-tier client/server environment with a Visual Basic ODBC client and
   a database server on any of a wide range of multivendor platforms and
   databases.

o  A three-tier client/server environment with a Visual Basic client and an
   ACMS server application on OpenVMS Alpha systems.

o  A three-tier client/server environment with a Visual Basic client and an
   ACMSxp server application on DEC OSF/1 systems.

Users can move into client/server application development with a step by
step approach, utilizing Digital's RMS (Record Management System) Gateway,
and Visual Basic functionality to obtain data from RMS files. Also, users
can re-engineer applications to take advantage of the client/server
application architecture.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DECADMIRE V2.1 and DECADMIRE V2.1 for Visual Basic are available now through
Digital, its DECdirect service, its resellers, and Microsoft catalogs.
Users who purchase DECADMIRE V2.1 for Visual Basic with service upgrades
will receive V3.0 when it becomes available.

