POLYCENTER Advanced File System and Utilities V3.2 for DEC OSF/1

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Both base AdvFS and the layered AdvFS Utilities are updated

o  The popular GUI is now even easier to use

o  Supports DEC OSF/1 V3.2

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

V3.2 of the POLYCENTER Advanced File System (AdvFS) and Utilities is a
maintenance release including software fixes, performance enhancements, and
miscellaneous enhancements to the popular AdvFS GUI (graphical user
interface). Both the base portion of AdvFS, which is packaged with DEC OSF/1
software, and the layered AdvFS Utilities are updated in V3.2. Enhancements
to the base AdvFS include an increase in the limit of mounted filesets from
256 to 512, plus miscellaneous fixes.

Enhancements to the AdvFS Utilities are primarily visible in the GUI, and
include:

o  Improved usability -- Improved error handling, additional operations
   (such as renaming a fileset), and improved interactions based on
   usability testing feedback.

o  Re-scanning -- Users can now re-scan volumes, file domains, and filesets
   without exiting and restarting the GUI. For example, if a new hot-plug
   drive is added in a StorageWorks cabinet, simply click a button to
   re-scan the available volumes and the new disk appears.

o  Expanded alerts display -- View all alerts for all file domains at once,
   instead of being limited to viewing one file domain at a time.

o  Expanded cross-application launching -- Invoke the Logical Storage
   Manager (LSM) and POLYCENTER Networker Save and Restore from the main
   window's Tools menu without leaving the AdvFS GUI. Users can even add
   their own tools to the Tools menu.

A prerequisite to the AdvFS Utilities is the base AdvFS, which is packaged
at no extra cost with the DEC OSF/1 operating system. Both the base AdvFS
V3.2 and the AdvFS Utilities V3.2 support DEC OSF/1 V3.2. The AdvFS
Utilities are included at a discount in the NAS 200, 250, and 300 packages.
Users who receive V3.2 of the DEC OSF/1 operating system before they receive
the updated Complementary Products CD-ROM (which has been delayed slightly),
can use V3.0 of the AdvFS Utilities on DEC OSF/1 V3.2, until they receive
the complementary CD-ROM containing AdvFS Utilities V3.2.

BENEFITS

The AdvFS and Utilities provide a rapid-restart, online-reconfigurable file
system that greatly complements DEC OSF/1 software in a production system
environment. With AdvFS, users no longer need to wait for hours while their
file systems recover from a system failure. Also, they do not need to bring
the system down in order to reconfigure their file system partitions,
defragment files, or clone a file system for hot backup.

The AdvFS and Utilities complement Digital's other storage management and
high availability products. For example, rapid restart decreases failover
time in the DECsafe Available Server Environment; files can be migrated to
POLYCENTER HSM optical storage; and online resize complements the
StorageWorks products. In addition, the AdvFS is launchable from POLYCENTER
NetView Manager.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The POLYCENTER Advanced File System and Utilities V3.2 will be available in
March. Note that the UPI for these products is "zero EG."

