TeamRoute for ALL-IN-1 V1.3

HIGHLIGHTS

o  OpenVMS Alpha support added

o  Server version can be installed on any language version of ALL-IN-1 V1.3

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital's solution for mail-enabled administrative workflow is TeamRoute
software. TeamRoute for ALL-IN-1 software is capable of routing any document
stored in an ALL-IN-1 Office Server file cabinet to any user on the network.
Documents can include forms, word processing documents, images, CAD
drawings, spreadsheets, and more. The originator of the routed item
specifies the routing list, and the document is then routed in the order
specified.

During the review process, each reviewer is granted specific processing
rights or requirements based on roles. By assigning roles, the originator
can selectively specify privileges for actions to be taken by any reviewer
on the document. For example, the right to add or remove additional
reviewers may be granted.

As a document is processed, its actual location and status may be determined
by anyone on the routing list who has been assigned this role.  This
capability enables users to dramatically decrease the time spent tracking
documents during the review cycle.

TeamRoute for ALL-IN-1 V1.3 (33.75.03) is available for use with only the
ALL-IN-1 Office Server V3.1 release. TeamRoute for ALL-IN-1 V1.3 supports
three clients -- TeamLinks Routing for Windows, TeamLinks Routing for
Macintosh, and the ALL-IN-1 VT user client.

New features of TeamRoute for ALL-IN-1 V1.3 include:

o  Support for OpenVMS Alpha platforms.

o  Support for ALL-IN-1 Office Server V3.1.

o  Ability to be installed on any language version of ALL-IN-1 V3.1 so that
   any TeamLinks Routing client will be able to use the routing server.

BENEFITS

o  ALL-IN-1 and TeamLinks Server solution can now take advantage of the
   power and reduced cost of ownership of the Alpha platform.

o  Administrative workflow helps reduce the time and costs of many typical
   administrative processes, such as purchase order review and approval,
   expense reporting, travel authorizations, and document review.

